invariant: INV-17
file: widemul.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: widemul_p256_point_mul no longer calls p256_wide_wipe_below after
  the wide call. Every object that call names is still wiped, so the
  vectors and the residue checks on arm64 pass: what stays is whatever
  the compiler spilled of the scalar and every multiple of the point the
  ladder held, in the frames under the dispatcher's caller.
  bin/p256_equiv_test calls each dispatcher over a painted stack and
  requires zero where the wipe's array lay.

--- old
        p256_wide_mul(o, k, p);
        p256_wide_wipe_below();
--- new
        p256_wide_mul(o, k, p);
